=== NSEXEC POP-ORDER FIX 2026-11-22 (Linux VM Ubuntu 24.04, SDK 8.0.428) ===
Root cause verified against official NSIS wiki "NsExec plug-in" (nsis.sourceforge.io/NsExec_plug-in): ExecToStack pushes the return value on top of the stack and the printed output below it — first Pop = exit code, second Pop = output. The shipped 0.2.0 installer popped them backwards at all 10 ExecToStack sites, so the Ollama poll could never succeed; the user's real Windows run failed with "Ollama did not start (its local API did not answer within ~30 seconds)" even though `ollama list` showed qwen3.5:4b 3.3 GB. Same inversion broke RAM detection (always 4 GB fallback), disk-space check (silently skipped), Ollama size check, model verification and health check (could never pass). InnoSetup.iss audited: no equivalent bug — Inno Exec() returns Boolean and writes the exit code to the Code var; all uses check Code or file contents.
Fix: AuroraOperator.nsi — all 10 sites now Pop $0 (exit code) first; wrong comment corrected; header documents the fix. New tests/AuroraOperator.Tests/NsisInstallerTests.cs (5 cases).
