=== MODEL-NOT-FOUND FIX 2026-11-22 (Linux VM Ubuntu 24.04, SDK 8.0.428, ~/.dotnet/dotnet) ===
Real-world failure (user PC, first successful Windows run ~01:00 PKT): installer installed, app opened, connected to Ollama (localhost:11434); user typed "hi" and got only a local summary because Ollama /api/chat returned 404 {"error":"model 'qwen3:4b' not found"} — PC has qwen3.5:4b installed, not qwen3:4b. App fell back silently.
Fix: new ModelNotFoundException (404 model-not-found is a distinct outcome, chat/generate/streaming; 404 without that body stays a plain failure); new ModelFallback (pure selection: catalog priority qwen3:4b, qwen3:1.7b, qwen3:0.6b, qwen3:8b, qwen3.5:2b, qwen2.5-coder:3b, then installed non-catalog qwen-family first e.g. qwen3.5:4b, null when nothing installed; merged Model Manager list marking non-catalog installed models); ModelManager.GetAvailableModelsAsync + ResolveFallbackModelAsync; AgentEngine falls back transparently on ModelNotFound, retries with the installed model, says plainly which model was used and why + exact `ollama pull <model>` command, reports clearly when nothing is installed (no fabricated answer); fallback is session-only, never rewrites the persisted default; engine model now mutable via UpdateModel (a Model Manager switch previously did nothing until app restart). MainViewModel: merged Model Manager list, Switch persists the default (preferences) + updates the running engine, Download now asks approval first (ExternalCommunication, exact `ollama pull <model>` shown), status bar reports a session fallback; App.xaml.cs loads the saved default at startup; MainWindow.xaml merged labels + help text.
Tests: new tests/AuroraOperator.Tests/ModelNotFoundTests.cs (17 cases, all PASS) + 1 updated test in OllamaPhase7Tests.cs (404 model-not-found now expects ModelNotFoundException).
